# ---------------------------------------------------------------- runtime data
# The database holds real accounts, password hashes and live auth tokens.
# events.jsonl holds location history. Neither belongs in a public repo.
server/*.db
server/*.db-wal
server/*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
events.jsonl

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# nigehban-app/google-services.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is Firebase
# *client* config, not a credential -- the API key inside is restricted to the
# package name plus signing certificate. EAS Build does not upload gitignored
# files, so ignoring it produces a build with FCM silently missing and push
# dead. Committing it is also what lets a teammate build from a clean checkout.
# The FCM service-account key (the JSON with "private_key") is the real secret;
# that lives in EAS credentials and must never be committed.
GoogleService-Info.plist
# The FCM V1 service-account key -- the JSON containing "private_key". Unlike
# google-services.json above this is a real credential: it can send push as
# this Firebase project to every installed handset. It belongs in EAS
# credentials only. Ignored by name here because the natural mistake is to
# drop it next to app.json so `eas credentials` can find it, and EAS Build
# uploads everything that is not ignored.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
service-account*.json
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# -------------------------------------------------------------- dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/releases

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ JS build
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
*.jsbundle
*.hbc

# The generated native folders are ignored by nigehban-app/.gitignore, where
# `/android` and `/ios` are anchored to the app directory. Do not re-add them
# here unanchored: `android/` matches at any depth, which silently swallowed
# modules/nigehban-alarm/android/ -- handwritten Kotlin, not generated output --
# and it never reached git or the EAS upload, so it was never compiled in.

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- Arduino
nigehban_band_nrf52/build/
nigehban_band_nrf52/*.bin
nigehban_band_nrf52/*.elf
nigehban_band_nrf52/*.map
nigehban_band_nrf52/*.uf2
firmware/*/build/

